1412	/// `GET /-/v1/search?text=...&size=...` — npm search v1 endpoint.
1413	///
1414	/// Local-only: scans the on-disk storage and matches package names
1415	/// as a case-insensitive substring on `text`. Matches verdaccio's
1416	/// default behavior. We deliberately do NOT proxy to upstream npm
1417	/// even in proxy mode — the tests rely on the local-search semantics
1418	/// (`releasing/commands/test/search.ts` asserts that a guaranteed-not
1419	/// -to-exist query returns "No packages found", which an upstream
1420	/// proxy can't deliver because npm's search is fuzzy and returns
1421	/// dozens of unrelated matches for almost anything).
1422	///
1423	/// Results are filtered by the per-package access policy: a package
1424	/// the caller can't read (e.g. anonymous + `@private/*` or
1425	/// `@pnpm.e2e/needs-auth` with the default rules) is dropped from
1426	/// `objects` before the response is built. Without this the search
1427	/// endpoint would happily enumerate protected packages that the
1428	/// packument and tarball GETs correctly hide behind 401.
1429	async fn serve_search(state: &AppState, headers: &HeaderMap, query_string: &str) -> Response {
